<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:vm="using:Patterns.App.ViewModels"
             x:Class="Patterns.App.Views.Sections.WebSection"
             x:DataType="vm:MainViewModel">

  <StackPanel Classes="form" Margin="4,8,12,16">
    <TextBlock Classes="h1 neon-remote" Text="Remote &amp; web" />

    <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="REMOTE CONTROL" />
    <CheckBox Content="Remote control on (web remote + Companion)" IsChecked="{Binding State.Control.Enabled}" />
    <CheckBox Content="Remotes may ARM the cue stack (CUE ARM ON / OFF, the Companion ARM key)" IsChecked="{Binding State.Control.RemotesMayArm}"
              ToolTip.Tip="Off by default: arming is a deliberate act at the desk. GO, standby and HOLD from a remote need the stack armed either way." />
    <StackPanel IsEnabled="{Binding State.Control.Enabled}">
      <Grid ColumnDefinitions="130,*,16,Auto,8,90">
        <TextBlock Classes="label" Text="Web remote port" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        <NumericUpDown Grid.Column="1" Minimum="1024" Maximum="65535" Increment="1" FormatString="0"
                       Value="{Binding State.Control.HttpPort, Mode=TwoWay, Converter={StaticResource Num}}" />
        <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" Classes="label" Text="Companion (TCP)" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        <NumericUpDown Grid.Column="5" Minimum="1024" Maximum="65535" Increment="1" FormatString="0"
                       Value="{Binding State.Control.TcpPort, Mode=TwoWay, Converter={StaticResource Num}}" />
      </Grid>
      <TextBlock Classes="label" Text="Open on a phone or tablet on this network:" Margin="0,4,0,0" />
      <TextBox Text="{Binding RemoteUrlsText, Mode=OneWay}" IsReadOnly="True" AcceptsReturn="True"
               FontFamily="Consolas,monospace" />
      <TextBlock Classes="hint tip"
                 Text="The web remote drives presenter next/back, looks, transport, blackout, screens, the audio track, lower thirds and the web page on air — big buttons, made for a phone at the tech table or in a pocket. Bitfocus Companion: add a 'Patterns' connection with the companion module (integrations folder in the repo), or use Generic TCP with the commands in docs/REMOTE.md — looks, screens, canvas groups and page actions map straight onto Stream Deck keys with live feedback. No password: anyone on this network can control the show while enabled." />

      <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="OSC" />
      <CheckBox Content="OSC in (UDP) — QLab, TouchOSC, a lighting desk, Companion's OSC" IsChecked="{Binding State.Control.OscEnabled}"
                ToolTip.Tip="Off by default: another open port is a deliberate act. Every address starts /patterns/ and means exactly the TCP line it maps to" />
      <Grid ColumnDefinitions="130,90,16,Auto,8,*,8,90" IsEnabled="{Binding State.Control.OscEnabled}">
        <TextBlock Classes="label" Text="OSC port" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        <NumericUpDown Grid.Column="1" Minimum="1024" Maximum="65535" Increment="1" FormatString="0" ShowButtonSpinner="False"
                       Value="{Binding State.Control.OscPort, Mode=TwoWay, Converter={StaticResource Num}}" ToolTip.Tip="The UDP port Patterns listens on" />
        <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" Classes="label" Text="Feedback to" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        <TextBox Grid.Column="5" Text="{Binding State.Control.OscFeedbackHost, Mode=TwoWay}" Watermark="host or address — empty = no feedback"
                 ToolTip.Tip="Every change sends one bundle of /patterns/state/… messages here (the tablet running TouchOSC, the desk running Companion); replies to a command go to whoever sent it either way" />
        <NumericUpDown Grid.Column="7" Minimum="1" Maximum="65535" Increment="1" FormatString="0" ShowButtonSpinner="False"
                       Value="{Binding State.Control.OscFeedbackPort, Mode=TwoWay, Converter={StaticResource Num}}" ToolTip.Tip="The port the feedback host listens on" />
      </Grid>
      <TextBlock Classes="label" Text="{Binding OscStatus}" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
      <TextBlock Classes="hint tip"
                 Text="Addresses: /patterns/outputs 1|0 · /patterns/blackout [1|0] · /patterns/identify · /patterns/look n|name · /patterns/next, /prev · /patterns/screen/n [1|0] · /patterns/lock/n [1|0] · /patterns/group/A 1|0 · /patterns/audio/play, /stop · /patterns/music/play [n|name], /pause, /next, /volume level · /patterns/tone 1|0 · /patterns/duck [1|0] · /patterns/stinger n|name, /stinger/stop, /vog, /sting · /patterns/lowerthird n|name [person], /lowerthird/off · /patterns/person n|name · /patterns/web/key key|action [page], /web/next, /prev, /present, /play…, /web/click x y, /web/type text, /web/reload, /web/open address · /patterns/section n|name · /patterns/stream 1|0 · /patterns/cue/go [id], /cue/standby/next, /prev, /cue/standby number|name, /cue/hold 1|0, /cue/arm 1|0 · /patterns/stopall · /patterns/ping. A number or a name rides as the next address segment or as the first argument; a switch is 1/0, a float above 0.5, a bool, or on/off/toggle; a fader's 0.0–1.0 float is a music level. A refused command answers /patterns/error to the sender, ping answers /patterns/pong. The feedback bundle carries /patterns/state/live, /blackout, /program, /duck, /tone, /audio, /music, /music/now, /music/level, /stinger, /stinger/hold, /lowerthird, /lowerthird/person, /stream, /playlist, /health, /rev, /screen/n, /lock/n, /cue/armed, /cue/hold, /cue/confirm, /cue/standby (number, name), /cue/previous, /cue/next, /cue/last (number, outcome), /cue/offset, /cue/follow. The full list with the meanings is in docs/REMOTE.md." />
    </StackPanel>

    <TextBlock Classes="hint tip"
               Text="Watchdog, performance monitoring, GPU choice and machine health live on the Machine page (ADMIN)." />

    <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="A WEB PAGE ON THE PATTERN" />
    <TextBlock Classes="hint tip"
               Text="Session schedules, dashboards, wayfinding, a YouTube video, a Google Slides deck, a PowerPoint on Office 365: paste the address and put it on the pattern. It renders inside the engine — it joins spans and trims, reaches NDI and the stream, rides with looks and cues, takes clicks, keys and typing from the desk — and nothing opens outside Patterns. A YouTube, Vimeo or Slides link goes on as the player or the deck alone." />
    <TextBox Watermark="https://example.com/schedule — a YouTube, Vimeo, Google Slides or PowerPoint link — or a local HTML file" Text="{Binding State.Web.Url}" />
    <WrapPanel Margin="0,4,0,0">
      <Button Classes="go" Content="SHOW THIS PAGE ON THE PATTERN" Command="{Binding PutWebPageOnPatternCommand}" Margin="0,0,8,6"
              ToolTip.Tip="The selected target's pattern becomes a Media pattern showing this page inside the engine — spans, NDI, the stream, looks and cues all carry it; drive it on the PREVIEW pane and with the PAGE CONTROLS on the Media page" />
    </WrapPanel>
    <TextBlock Classes="hint tip"
               Text="Inside the engine the page is a picture like any other: it fits the canvas, crossfades, sits under the overlays and the lower third, and can be a layer over another pattern too (Media page → LAYERS → Web page). Click, drag and scroll it on the PREVIEW pane; PAGE CONTROLS on the Media page type into it and carry the page's own actions (NEXT, PRESENT, PLAY…); KEYS → PAGE hands it the whole keyboard; the pointer is drawn for the room or hidden per page. The same actions run from cues, the wire, OSC, the phone and Companion. Needs the WebView2 runtime, which Windows 10 and 11 keep current." />

    <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="SAVED PAGES" />
    <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding State.Web.SavedUrls}">
      <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
        <DataTemplate x:DataType="x:String">
          <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,6,Auto,Auto" Margin="0,2">
            <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{Binding}" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" ToolTip.Tip="{Binding}" />
            <Button Grid.Column="2" Classes="mini" Content="Use"
                    ToolTip.Tip="Put this address in the page box"
                    Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:MainViewModel)DataContext).LoadWebUrlCommand}"
                    CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
            <Button Grid.Column="3" Classes="mini" Content="✕"
                    Command="{Binding $parent[UserControl].((vm:MainViewModel)DataContext).RemoveWebUrlCommand}"
                    CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
          </Grid>
        </DataTemplate>
      </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
    </ItemsControl>

    <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="GOOD TO KNOW" />
    <TextBlock Classes="hint tip"
               Text="Every page lives inside the engine and is driven from the desk, a cue, the phone or a Stream Deck; a link that wants a new window opens in the same page instead, so the show never leaves Patterns. A page with sound plays it on the default device unless muted (Media page → SOUND). PowerPoint for the web and a Google Slides deck of your own need a sign-in once: KEYS → PAGE on the Media page, type, and the account stays signed in on this machine." />
  </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
